Next slide.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.310
I might just quickly motivate

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:55.240
why we're focused on adolescents.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:58.580
Why is this sort of an
interesting group to look at

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:02.010
particularly in refugee contexts?

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:05.210
So adolescence is a time where physical

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:08.300
transformations are large, right?

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:10.740
They're going through puberty.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:15.220
And in addition, children's
place in the household

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.320
trains is dramatically and
it changes very differently

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.530
for boys and girls, right?

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:21.352
Gender norm has become
more, much more salient

00:09:21.352 --> 00:09:22.185
than this time.

00:09:22.185 --> 00:09:24.256
It's also time adolescents are probably

00:09:24.256 --> 00:09:25.089
vulnerable to a wide range

00:09:25.089 --> 00:09:27.160
of risk-taking behavior that could

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.960
jeopardize long-term outcomes.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.480
But this sort of malleability also ensures

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:36.058
that this is a time where intervention

00:09:36.058 --> 00:09:39.390
maybe particularly salient is why

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:42.536
and so why we search this
investor have now called

00:09:42.536 --> 00:09:44.643
on adolescents has kind
of a window of opportunity

00:09:44.643 --> 00:09:45.476
for intervention, right?

00:09:45.476 --> 00:09:47.520
So building on the first, 1000 days to say

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.700
this is another key touch
point where intervention

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:54.700
may be critical to
promote improved outcomes

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:58.780
as adolescent age, you think, you know

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:03.040
reaching adolescents,
not only because of the

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:07.230
there are sort of the
importance to good outcomes

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:10.000
in adulthood, but adolescents
are also a massive proportion

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.080
of the population, right?

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:12.620
And that's growing.

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:16.120
So reaching adolescents
is going to be critical

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:19.200
for achieving the sustainable
development goals.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.880
And so we really need to understand more

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:24.100
about their lives across various contexts.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:24.933
Next slide.

