health issues are one

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:26.936
of the leading causes of
disability among adolescents with

00:13:26.936 --> 00:13:30.370
I think alongside, I'm going to forget

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.820
but basically it's one
of the top three causes.

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:35.350
And so we know, and we
also know that the majority

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:36.680
of mental health illnesses

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:38.870
in adulthood start in adolescence.

00:13:38.870 --> 00:13:41.759
And so we can see how these
sort of negative shocks

00:13:41.759 --> 00:13:44.940
from violence leading to higher symptoms

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:47.260
of psychosocial distress

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:51.740
and adolescents can then lead
to longer term consequences.

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:55.850
And Jennifer is gonna speak
directly to the association

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:59.090
between past exposure to violence
and current mental health.

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:01.410
And then just finally, I think
the other point is, you know

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:04.800
we increasingly recognize the importance

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:06.730
of nutrition during adolescents

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:08.980
and there's a lot sort of
innovative new research

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:10.910
around an adolescent growth spurt, right?

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:12.250
So if you've missed out in childhood

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:14.301
you may actually be able to catch

00:14:14.301 --> 00:14:16.760
up if you intervene
appropriately, we had adolescent.

